{
  "requirement": "`habeas_sdk::graph` MUST expose the graph's associated types and content lookup operation:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Graph: Send + Sync {\n    type NodeId: Clone + Eq + Send + Sync;\n    type NodeContent: Send + Sync;\n    type EdgeLabel: Clone + Send + Sync;\n    type Error: Send;\n\n    // Outgoing edges and judgment metadata are specified separately.\n    fn node_content(&self, node: &Self::NodeId) -> Result<Self::NodeContent, Self::Error>;\n}\n```\n\nThe SDK MUST leave the domain meaning of node identities, edges, and contents\nto the consumer.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations derived from `requirements.sdk.graph.domain_types`**\n1. `habeas_sdk::graph::Graph` exposes `NodeId`, `NodeContent`, `EdgeLabel` and `Error`, with the stated bounds.\n2. `Graph` exposes `node_content(&self, &NodeId) -> Result<NodeContent, Error>`.\n3. The SDK leaves the domain meaning of node identities, edges and contents to the consumer.\n\n**Coverage of the type-shape obligation**\n- The bounds are checked by the compiler at each `impl Graph`. The reviewed tests implement `Graph` for many unrelated consumer domains, so the trait must accept all of them:\n  - `Memory` in `agent.rs`, with `Node`, `Contents`, `Label` and `io::Error`.\n  - `GraphOnly` in `contracts.rs`, with `Node`, `Content`, `u8` and `&'static str`.\n  - `Memory` in `validation.rs`, with `u8`, `String`, `u8` and `&'static str`.\n  - `StoredGraph` in `storage.rs`, with `String`, `()`, `()` and `FileStorageError`.\n  - `GraphWithChangingEdges` in `agent.rs`, with `u8`, `String`, `()` and `io::Error`.\n  - `HabeasDomain` and `ReviewGraph`, with `HabeasNode`, `ResolvedInput`/`Value`, `HabeasEdgeLabel` and `io::Error`.\n- The `send` helper in `checker_needs_no_validation_and_storage_preserves_nonserializable_metadata` also checks that a consumer's futures are `Send`.\n\n**Coverage of `node_content`**\n- Success results are asserted in the following tests:\n  - `requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk` reads `changed.node_content(&source_node)` and asserts its fingerprint changes when the source changes.\n  - `review_graph_delegates_unprepared_sources_and_paths_to_the_domain` compares the delivered input with `graph.domain().node_content(&source)` and asserts that the content contains `call();`.\n  - `default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix` checks the content reaches the dependency fingerprint and the chat history.\n  - `validation_is_usable_without_any_evidence_storage` checks the content reaches the dependency fingerprint.\n- Failure results are asserted in two tests:\n  - `review_graph_delegates_unprepared_sources_and_paths_to_the_domain` asserts that reading the missing `fn[missing]` node is an error and records no dependency.\n  - `checker_needs_no_validation_and_storage_preserves_nonserializable_metadata` injects a `\"read\"` failure and asserts the consumer's own `Error` value comes back unchanged.\n\n**Coverage of \"meaning left to the consumer\"**\n- `habeas_paths_preserve_opaque_segments_and_separate_all_node_kinds` shows the SDK treats the consumer's node identities as opaque.\n- The several unrelated domains listed above, each with its own node, edge and content types, show the SDK does not impose any meaning on them.\n\n**Gaps**\nI found no untested obligation, and I found no wrong expected result. There is no `{fixme}` acknowledgment, and none is needed.",
  "references": "00a6c109c5ae23ac2c87dc0627d20dcf1d3101a5c1eb749cecc1db614e8e1143",
  "inputs": [
